--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party code and attribution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Parts of the model implementation follow, or are adapted from, published work
by others.

* ST-GCN architecture: the ten-block spatio-temporal stack, the 9-frame
  temporal unit, and the edge-importance mask.
  Yan, Xiong & Lin, "Spatial Temporal Graph Convolutional Networks for
  Skeleton-Based Action Recognition", AAAI 2018.
  https://github.com/yysijie/st-gcn  --  BSD-2-Clause.

* STGCN++ multi-branch temporal unit: six branches (1x1 convolution,
  max-pool, four dilated 3-frame convolutions).
  Duan et al., "PYSKL: Towards Good Practices for Skeleton Action
  Recognition".
  https://github.com/kennymckormick/pyskl  --  Apache-2.0.

* Graph-learning modes "none" / "init" / "offset" / "importance": the names,
  semantics and initialisations mirror unit_gcn(adaptive=...).
  https://github.com/kennymckormick/pyskl
  https://github.com/open-mmlab/mmaction2  --  both Apache-2.0.

* Direction-partitioned adjacency (self / inward / outward links),
  reimplemented in PyTorch.
  Shi et al., "Two-Stream Adaptive Graph Convolutional Networks for
  Skeleton-Based Action Recognition", CVPR 2019.
  https://github.com/lshiwjx/2s-AGCN  --  no licence declared upstream; the
  implementation here is independent and cites the method.

